<title>UK: Gallaher opens trading at 282-1/2p.</title>
<headline>Gallaher opens trading at 282-1/2p.</headline>
<dateline>LONDON 1997-05-30</dateline>
<text>
<p>Gallaher Group Plc began its first day of trade on the London Stock Exchange at 282-1/2p per share, valuing Britain's largest manufacturer of tobacco products at around 1.95 billion stg.</p>
<p>Gallaher, whose leading brands include Benson and Hedges and Silk Cut cigarettes as well as Hamlet Cigars and Old Holborn handrolling tobacco, also started unconditional dealings in American Depository Securities (ADS) on the New York Stock Exchange at 1330 GMT/0930EDT.</p>
<p>The stock market had expected an issue price of 310p to 320p, but shortly before trading began the FTSE 100 fell 70.0 points, or 1.5 percent, to 4,602.3.</p>
<p>--London Newsroom +44 171 542 5106</p>
